  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=8,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[4X+3].$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=4$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4X+3] & ={4}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =16\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
